# Cursor Editor — Skills System

## Overview

Cursor Skills are markdown files that teach the agent how to perform specific tasks: reviewing PRs using team standards, generating commit messages in a preferred format, querying database schemas, or any specialized workflow. Skills provide structured, repeatable knowledge that the agent can apply consistently.

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Storage Locations"
        P[Personal Skills<br/>~/.cursor/skills/]
        PROJ[Project Skills<br/>.cursor/skills/]
        BI[Built-in Skills<br/>~/.cursor/skills-cursor/]
    end
    
    subgraph "Skill Structure"
        S[skill-name/]
        S --> SK[SKILL.md - Required<br/>Main instructions]
        S --> RM[reference.md - Optional<br/>Detailed documentation]
        S --> EX[examples.md - Optional<br/>Usage examples]
        S --> SC[scripts/ - Optional<br/>Utility scripts]
    end
    
    P --> S
    PROJ --> S
    BI --> S
```

